# Aerius Challenge - Team Code-6

Autonomous drone navigation (ArduPilot SITL + Gazebo, 16-beam LiDAR).

## How it works
- reads the lidar and splits the surroundings into 5 degree sectors
- sectors with obstacles are blocked (with some extra margin for drone size)
- drone flies towards the free sector closest to the goal direction
- slows down near obstacles, backs off if something is very close
- if it gets stuck for a while it tries to go around from the other side
- lands after reaching the goal

## Requirements
python3, numpy, pymavlink, ROS 2 (rclpy, sensor_msgs). Nothing extra.

## Run
Start Gazebo + SITL first, then

    python3 navigate.py

Settings (goal, speed, altitude, mavlink port) are at the top of `navigate.py`.
